# Someone who supports or heralds the establishment of a [[utopia]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Arthur Kissam Train|title=The Story of Everyday Things|year=1941|publisher=Harper & Brothers|page=390|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/storyofeverydayt00trai/page/390/mode/1up|passage=One of our brighter young '''Utopians''', Aldous Huxley, predicts that the movies of the future will include “feelies” and “smellies.”}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 29, 2007|author=Michiko Kakutani|title=The Cult of the Amateur|work=New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2007/06/29/books/29book.html
|passage=Digital '''utopians''' have heralded the dawn of an era in which Web 2.0 {{...|— distinguished by a new generation of participatory sites like MySpace.com and YouTube.com, which emphasize user-generated content, social networking and interactive sharing —}} ushers in the democratization of the world: more information, more perspectives, more opinions, more everything, and most of it without filters or fees.}}

